hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17601","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, and 'Abd al-Razzaq [said]: Sufyan informed us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah. 'Abd al-Razzaq said: al-Tamimi, meaning Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah al-Fihri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third after the fifth."
"17602","'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grant a third."
"17603","'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah al-Tamimi, who said: Habib ibn Maslamah narrated to me, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grant a third."
"17604","Hammad ibn Khalid, and he is al-Khayyat, narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, from al-'Ala' ibn al-Harith, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a fourth after the fifth on the outward expedition and granted a third after the fifth on the return."
"17605","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz: Makhul narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third after the fifth."
"17606","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grant a third after the fifth."
"17607","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, from Makhul, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a third after the fifth."
"17608","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Jariyah, from Habib ibn Maslamah, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grant a fourth at the outset and a third on the return. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: There is no man in Sham more sound in hadith than Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, meaning al-Tanukhi."
